      "writtenOn": "2021-07-16T03:40:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, in theory, we do have cases to have multiple SignalRequestRecord that have same live token: for example, when the same client call twice #setSignalStrengthUpdateRequest with same SignalStrengthUpdateRequest but with different subId.\n\nSince subId is different, we store both request in mSignalRequestRecords. They share the same SSURequest, the token is the same. Calling clearSignalStrengthUpdateRequest will clean both of them.",
      "parentUuid": "6217a9f6_9f76c9ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 121,
        "endChar": 33
      },
